


/* auto_run */

/* by Reinhard Wimmer, Aalborg University, Denmark */

/* AU program to conrol automation with many options */

/* added support for wavemaker 1.7.2025   */

/* usage auto_run */
/*    auto_run uses loop counters L25-L29 as flags (arguments) :
 
		L25:
		  2: set O2 equal to O1 (after O1 has been set as determined by L26)

		L26:	0: O1 is taken from the parameter set (no adjustment)
			1: automated: like "0" for non-water solvents (incl D2O), like "2" for solvents mainly consisting of H2O
			2: like 4
			3: exectue macro set_O1 (use only if you have done o1calib.aal on the same sample immediately before)
			4: o1calib.bruker (automated adjustment of O1 by BRUKER method, saves O1 in macro set_O1 for later use)

		L27: 1: shimming is controlled by ICON-NMR (default)
		     2: force 1D-topshim before experiment
		     3: force 3D-topshim, followed by 1D-topshim, before experiment
		L28:
			0: no pulsecal, no getprosol
			1: no pulsecal, only getprosol
			2: pulsecal
			3: pulsecal sn
			4: execute macro set_P1 (contains a getprosol statement written by pulsecal.aal. Only use if you have done pulsecal
			on that very sample immediately before)
			5: do 4 first, then run wavemaker (wvm -a)
			
		L29:
			0: no RGA (use onlyfor COSY), RG is set as parameter
			1: execute RGA prior to measurement 

*/

/* other specialties to be considered

13C-decoupling: control the duration of AQ
if USERA4 contains the term 'aqmax', then the total length of AQ (acquisition time) is limited
The user has to pass the maximum allowed AQ as CNST12 in units of seconds.
the automation will check the current AQ set and compare to CNST12. If AQ>CNST12, AQ will be reduced
OBS: This will not check for the decoupling power, nor decoupling that might occur in the middle of the sequence.
It only checks the duration of AQ.


high temperature (>50C)
the automation will not allow setting the temperature >50C.


DOSY:
if USERA4 contains the term 'dosy', then 
xau dosy 5 {CNST11} {TD1} l n n
is executed.
5 is the starting gradient strength (in %)
CNST11 is the maximum gradient strength (in %) to be reached during the DOSY experiment (e.g. 95)
TD1 is the number of datapoints in the indirect dimension
l is linear ramp
n no RGA
n no aq start

running without lock: 2H-acquisition
the automation will check whether there is a lock, before starting ZG. Without lock, the acquisition will be skipped.
In special cases (e.g. 2H-aqcuisition), the spectrum has to be recorded without lock.
this can be done by including the term 'nolock' into USERA4

z-shim correction:
due to temperature gradients in the sample, the z-shim given by topshim is not always optimal
if you know the correction, you can do the following
if USERA4 contains 'shimcorr' then the value contained in CNST13 is added to the z-shim after topshim and AUTOSHIM is deactivated

# from here downwards: added 1.7.2025 by RW

wavemaker:  
if the pulse program contains a selective pulse that is to be calculated by Wavemaker, include 'wvm' into USERA4
This will execute 'wvm -a' prior to acquisition
*/

